WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:09.480
I'd say, being in a blended family,
the hardest part is the beginning.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.320
It's war, it's emotional,
it's difficult.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:13.760
You're getting used to new people.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:15.560
Stepfamilies are born of loss.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:18.240
Coming together
and making a blended family work

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:21.760
and crossing that divide
into making it successful

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.040
is quite tricky.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:27.520
So you've met your partner, you're
really happy, you're moving on,

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.800
you're maybe moving in together -
things are going to be great.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:30.680
Or are they?

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:46.760
Don't expect it to be perfect,

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:50.440
don't expect the children
to love you immediately.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:52.000
The children have had losses.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:54.680
The children need to mourn
what used to be their family

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:55.800
and things have changed.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:58.440
Everything's moving
about and shifting

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.480
so give everybody time to do that.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:02.560
They will do so at their own pace.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:07.480
Don't expect them to be
where you are with your partner

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:09.920
recognising it takes,
probably four years

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.960
as the average,
for a stepfamily to form.

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:13.920
So don't rush things.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.160
You might have been together
two or three years

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:18.040
but you're still on a journey.

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:27.520
You may go into the stepfamily
as a stepparent

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.080
and assume you're
going to be something.

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:34.640
Maybe it's a surrogate mother. Maybe
you want to be the bonus mother.

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:38.200
Or maybe you want to be nothing
at all to those stepchildren

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:42.800
but also you're dealing with the
children's expectations of you.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:45.760
If I ask you what a mum
is supposed to do or a dad,

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:50.760
a biological mum or dad, most people
have a great idea - we all know.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.960
But if I ask the same people,
"What's a stepmum, what's a stepdad?"

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:56.560
I'd probably get different answers.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:58.040
My own research found that

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:02.040
stepmum's have significantly higher
anxiety than biological mums.

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:03.480
This confusion with role,

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:05.920
not knowing what they
were supposed to do.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.080
Were they supposed to take
more control in the house?

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:12.920
Were they supposed to be
more integrated with the children?

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.240
Leave the children
to the biological parent?

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:17.240
Think about what you're
comfortable doing.

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:20.240
Are you comfortable spending
more time with the children?

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:22.280
The important thing
is to talk to your partner.

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:24.440
Work out what role
you have in your family.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:27.960
There are no rights and wrongs but
it is important that you both agree.

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:36.480
With my stepsister
it took about a year

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:38.800
until we started feeling
like proper family.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.760
And I do consider her now
like a full sister.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:44.840
And someone I can go to
in a time of need.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:47.640
It probably, as well, took a year
until we started bickering,

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:50.880
like you do,
over clothes and shoes mainly.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:52.560
And I think that's
when you can really tell

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:54.200
that you're starting
to feel like a family -

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:56.680
when you feel like you can just
lose your rag at someone

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:58.200
if they borrow your crop top.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:01.480
Stepfamilies are often
very busy homes.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:04.320
There can be children
from both partners,

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.880
there can be children
from the new partnership,

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.960
they may not all get on,
again that's really common,

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:12.720
siblings don't necessarily get on.

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:16.160
Try finding ways
of engaging all the children

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:18.320
so try and develop something to do,

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:21.280
an activity with each of the children
so they can feel special,

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:24.560
they can develop a relationship
with both their parent,

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:27.080
their biological parent
and also their stepparent.

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:31.240
So find a thing to do,
it might be going out on a bike ride,

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:33.200
it might be making cakes together -

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:34.760
whatever works in your family.

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:37.840
Each family member
will come into this new family

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:41.680
with different memories, but you want
to make your own memories as a family

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:45.520
so bring everyone together and that
should start to bring everybody

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:46.880
to feel a sense of belonging.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.720
Some of you might have
heard the term 'Disney dad'

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:56.040
and it's a term that people use

00:03:56.120 --> 00:04:01.480
where the biological dad sees his
kids perhaps at weekends or holidays

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:05.400
and he feels that he's got
to make it the best time ever.

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:07.480
So his children are coming,
he's missed them

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:10.280
and he just wants to make up
for the time when he's not with them.

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:14.880
It can mean that that time
becomes just fun time

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:17.960
and that's not real
and it's not sustainable.

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:21.200
Don't let the children
be feeling that,

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:23.320
{\an2}"I'm only coming to Dad's because
of what he's going to give me,

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:24.360
there'll be a new present,

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:25.720
we're going to go
and do something great."

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:27.960
That shouldn't be the case,

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:30.360
it's fine to treat your children,
but not all the time.

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:39.600
When people ask me if I'm upset
about my parents divorcing

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:43.000
I would say no, never.

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:46.960
I'm so happy now my parents are happy
in respective relationships

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:51.280
and I gained a younger sister
and two older brothers,

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:54.560
and for me now, having that,

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:59.080
that's worth maybe a year or two
of some quite hard times,

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:02.120
but now I look back and I think,
well, that's great,

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:03.000
I've gained all of this.

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:05.680
Most stepfamilies have this
period where they're trying

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:07.720
to not be a stepfamily.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:10.320
They just want to blend in
and it's not about blending in -

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:12.520
it's about being who you are.

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:16.780
Enjoy it and you'll find
as you develop, as you integrate,

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:20.560
You'll find your own norm
and your own happiness.

